  "raw": {
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Parkville-Campus/Adjunct-Instructor---IS205-Managing-Information-Systems_JR100577": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor - IS205 Managing Information Systems",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nAppointments are made on a term-by-term basis. Adjunct faculty are required to successfully complete an online Canvas LMS orientation course before being scheduled, as well as other training if required by the department. This is a face to face course. Local applicants only.   Click on Park University Locations for more information on our campus centers. Click on Park University’s Catalog for more information on programs and courses. To ensure timely submission of your credentials, qualified applicants should apply following the specific instructions noted in each job posting. For all positions, a Masters Degree in the relevant field is required, along with related work and/or academic experience. For most postings, a Ph.D. or other terminal degree is preferred. Park University is an Equal Opportunity Employer encouraging applications from women and minorities. The university will recruit and employ qualified personnel and will provide equal opportunities during employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability or status as a qualified protected veteran. Click   here   to view Park University’s EEOC and related policies. Please Note: Park University participates in E-Verify for all positions at all campus center locations nationwide. Minimum Qualifications Masters or Ph.D. level degree in the discipline (CS or IS) or in a related discipline (MBA, etc.) from an accredited school AND received graduate credit with a grade of B or better in the course applied to teach, OR one year work experience in subject material of course applied to teach. The Computer Science department requires that you specifically address how professional   experience,   or graduate coursework pertains to   Core Learning Outcome   with   your   Questionnaire   subm ission .        Core Learning Outcomes: 1. Identify the skills that a manager of Information Systems requires to successfully lead a team in development and maintenance of an Information System. 2.  Compare various types of information systems,both traditional and modern. 3. Identify the strategic value of creating an information technology infrastructure and collaborative environment in various organizations. 4. Explain the impact of information technology on organizations and how to manage various aspects created by implementation of technology.  Course Description This course introduces the student to information systems concepts and the management concerns of information technology. The course focuses on the components, types, and management concerns of information systems which, when combined, support an enterprise. Students will explore the enterprise perspective on controlling the use of information systems and understanding project changes, risk, and quality management."
    },
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Parkville-Campus/Academic-Records---Athletic-Eligibility-Coordinator_JR100573": {
      "title": "Academic Records & Athletic Eligibility Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThis position serves as a front-line representative of the Registrar’s Office, providing high-quality customer service while supporting graduation, academic and athletic compliance, and student records operations. Working collaboratively across the office, the position performs a variety of functions related to graduation processing, commencement coordination, athletic eligibility, academic compliance, and records management to ensure the accuracy, integrity, and timely processing of student information. Primary responsibilities include processing diploma applications, verifying degree completion, supporting commencement activities, maintaining student records, certifying athletic eligibility, and providing data and support for the athletics department to support eligibility and academic progress. The position also provides general Registrar support and responds to inquiries from students, faculty, staff, and external constituents. Success in this role requires exceptional attention to detail, strong organizational and communication skills, sound judgment, and the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced, deadline-driven environment while maintaining the confidentiality of student records and adhering to FERPA, University policies, and applicable regulatory requirements. Position Accountabilities Graduation and Degree Processing (25%)   Assist with diploma application processing, degree audits, graduation verification, degree conferral preparation, diploma orders, and maintenance of graduation records. Review student records for completeness and identify discrepancies requiring further review.     Commencement Support (15%)   Assist with commencement planning and preparation, including participant lists, ceremony communications, commencement reports, ordering and distribution of graduation materials, and support for local commencement ceremonies.    Athletic Eligibility Support ( 4 0%)   Understand and apply academic eligibility rules and bylaws governing student-athletes. R eview and p rocess student-athlete eligibility records by compiling required documentation, evaluating eligibility status , preparing reports and maintaining records . Submit eligibility certificates to the NAIA. Communicate with NAIA , coaches, and athletic director regarding eligibility decisions and interpretation of academic eligibility bylaws. C oordinat e with Athletics and other University offices to support compliance with NAIA and institutional requirements. Provide GPAs of student-athletes and calculate team GPAs for scholar-athlete awards.    Academic Records and Departmental Support ( 10 %)   Compile, maintain , and distribute reports related to graduation, compliance, enrollment, and student records. Assist with data validation, record maintenance, and documentation to ensure accuracy and consistency across University systems.    Assist with office operations such as transcript processing, enrollment and degree verification, document imaging, grading support, maintenance of academic and demographic records , processing administrative withdrawal s , monitoring effective dates of withdrawals, and communicating outcomes to appropriate University stakeholders.   Participate in office projects, process improvements, cross-training initiatives, testing of new procedures, and other duties that support departmental and University objectives .     General Customer Service (10%)   Greet and assist all customers in a professional, courteous, and prompt manner. Respond to general inquiries (in person, phone, email) , including those related to graduation, commencement, and student records. Position Requirements: Associate degree or equivalent combination of education and experience required ; bachelor’s degree preferred.   1–2 years of related work experience required .   Strong computer literacy, including proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (especially Excel and Word), email platforms, and database/administrative systems.   Ability to understand, interpret and consistently apply academic policies and regulatory requirements .   Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to identify discrepancies and maintain accurate student records.   Experience working with student information systems, data validation, or compliance-related processes preferred.   Excellent written and verbal communication skills.   Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced, deadline-driven environment.   Ability to maintain confidentiality and adhere to FERPA and other applicable regulations.   Must be available for periodic overtime and participation in KC-area commencement ceremonies.   Founded in 1875, Park University is a private, liberal arts university. Park’s flagship campus is located in the Kansas City suburb of Parkville, Missouri, on the bluffs overlooking the Missouri River.  We offer an excellent benefits package including health, dental, and life insurance, retirement plan, and tuition-paid undergraduate classes for employees and dependents. Park University is an equal-opportunity employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Qualified applicants must upload a resume and cover letter that includes salary requirements."
    },
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Parkville-MO/Writing-Center-and-English-Language-Learner-Services-Coordinator_JR100567": {
      "title": "Writing Center and English Language Learner Services Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 24 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSince its founding in 1875, the diversity of our students has been central to the learning experience at Park University. In addition to serving traditionally aged, adult and military students, the University community includes a significant number of international students and permanent residents for whom English is not a native language. Reporting to the Director of Academic Retention Initiatives, this position coordinates the services Park provides to these English Language Learners. The purpose of this position is to coordinate services for all Park students who need specialized assistance in reading, speaking, and writing English for their Park University classes. These services include one-to-one and group tutoring, course-embedded tutoring, academic mentoring, and consulting with staff and faculty across the University. Position Accountabilities Coordinate Writing and ELL academic support services for undergraduate and graduate students across the Park University network, including training of professional and peer tutors and mentors Plan, develop, and implement a strategic plan that focuses on providing broad support for all Park students in writing and English language learning. Hiring, training, scheduling, and oversight of undergraduate/graduate peer tutoring staff and professional tutors in the Writing Center, for all modalities: Parkville, Gilbert, Campus Centers and Online. Create and present training and support resources to faculty in collaboration with academic program administrators and leaders within student life, student services, international education, writing across the curriculum, and faculty development programs Management of the day-to-day operations of the Writing Center, including overseeing the physical writing center (online writing center, and website; coordinating student orientation sessions and writing workshops; and creating various student and faculty writing resources. Development of innovative programming based on reflective assessment of the Writing Center and its services. Support of undergraduate student research and community engagement aligned with the Writing Center’s strategic plan. Coordination of promotion of services to students and faculty in conjunction with the other services in the Academic and Career Success Center Oversee the development, implementation, and continuous review of policies and practices of the Writing Center, including an assessment plan. Collaboration with academic departments and other units on campus, including the Park Writes, Office of International Programs, First Year Writing Program and Transformational Teaching and Learning Center. Oversee and train Writing and tutors and implement strategic writing and oral communication support for international and non-native English speakers. Beyond academic support, help students understand university policies and how to navigate course expectations. Perform other duties as assigned. Position Requirements: Master’s degree in English/Composition and Rhetoric, or related field with 3-5 years of professional experience working with students in an educational setting. Candidates with less experience may be considered, providing they have an earned specialized training in Writing Tutoring, ELL, English with ELL, ESL, TESOL, or related field Demonstrated understanding of best practices in tutoring writing, based on current writing center pedagogy and Writing Across the Curriculum philosophy. Analytical and organizational skills to understand, assess, and contribute to the development of programs and services Strong communication skills, both oral and written communication, to effectively interact with student, staff, and faculty stakeholders Cross-cultural knowledge, awareness, and empathy to facilitate student, staff, and faculty development Knowledge of higher education norms and expectations for student privacy and non-discrimination Preferred A minimum of two years of relevant Writing Center experience. Experience teaching university-level composition courses. A minor or certification in Teachers of English to Speakers of Other Languages (TESOL) to support diverse, multilingual student population. Scholarship in the field of Composition & Rhetoric, with emphasis in writing center theory and practice. Demonstrated efficacy as a teacher/tutor of undergraduate writers. Founded in 1875, Park University is a private, liberal arts university. Park’s flagship campus is located in the Kansas City suburb of Parkville, Missouri, on the bluffs overlooking the Missouri River.  We offer an excellent benefits package including health, dental, and life insurance, retirement plan, and tuition-paid undergraduate classes for employees and dependents. Park University is an equal-opportunity employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Qualified applicants must upload a resume and cover letter that includes salary requirements."
    },
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Parkville-MO/Return-of-Title-IV-Specialist_JR100536": {
      "title": "Return of Title IV Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-10\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Return to Title IV Specialist is a role within our Financial Aid division of Student Financial Services. This role is responsible for understanding and maintaining compliance within the function of Return of Title IV. This position is responsible for reviewing and understanding Federal Methodology as it pertains to R2T4, leading the R2T4 team within SFA in the areas of Return of Title IV adjustments, Reaffirmations, lender notifications, and “WF” grade report. Will have full working knowledge of all aspects of the drop and withdraw process; Will have full working knowledge of the complexities of R2T4 decision making in a module-heavy environment; Oversees completion of daily workload and resolves student issues when they require special handling; Manages the Satisfactory Academic Progress Appeal process from start to finish, making professional judgement decisions on these appeals independently; Assists other staff in the absence of the Associate Director, ensures completion of scheduled tasks within assigned deadlines, and assists in achieving departmental and organizational goals. This position is data-heavy with a full working knowledge of excel required. Position Accountabilities Maintaining compliance within the Return of Title IV (R2T4) function in a module based environment Leading the Return of Title IV team to ensure that goals and deadlines are met within the allowed error rate of less than 5% Processing the Return of Title IV calculations and aid adjustments Ensuring the integrity of the add/drop data and integration of that data into PowerFaids Processing of “WF” report at end of each session to process R2T4 on students who fail due to not completing the term Managing the reaffirmation process for students returning to attendance within a semester Ensure adjustments and returns are completed in a timely manner compliant with federal regulations Maintain professional working relationship with Registrar and Student Account departments Manages the Satisfactory Academic Progress Appeal process from start to finish, performing professional judgement decisions independently, working with students, Academic Success Center, and academic advisors to ensure student success following an appeal Assists Student Financial Aid Operations team in the absence of the Associate Director; this requires full knowledge of Title IV regulations and how they impact all functional areas of the financial aid office Other duties as assigned Position Requirements: Bachelor’s Degree required as position is compliance based. Previous experience in Return to Title IV is desired. Ability to work within complex data systems (CX/Jenzabar, PowerFaids). Expected to have a thorough ability to use Excel to manage data (ability to manipulate and interpret data using v-lookup, pivot tables, etc.). Leadership characteristics are required with the ability to hold self and coworkers to high standards in accuracy, deadlines, output, and compliance. Ability to train coworkers in Return to Title IV and other areas of expertise Ability to resolve problems and communicate professionally orally and in writing. Excellent interpersonal skills and ability to maintain good working relationships with outside departments. Ideal candidate would be committed to learning all aspects of the operations of Park Student Financial Aid. Strong orientation toward a high volume and fast-paced environment with demonstrated experience in compliance. Must be able to maintain exceptional level of accuracy while meeting tight deadlines. Previous experience in financial aid or equivalent combination of education and experience is required. Previous experience in Return to Title IV is desired Ability to work independently and make professional judgement decisions on SAP Appeals Ability to multitask, organize and establish priorities are required. Founded in 1875, Park University is a private, liberal arts university. Park’s flagship campus is located in the Kansas City suburb of Parkville, Missouri, on the bluffs overlooking the Missouri River.  We offer an excellent benefits package including health, dental, and life insurance, retirement plan, and tuition-paid undergraduate classes for employees and dependents. Park University is an equal-opportunity employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Qualified applicants must upload a resume and cover letter that includes salary requirements."
    },
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Gilbert-AZ/Recruitment-and-Admissions-Representative_JR100564": {
      "title": "Recruitment and Admissions Representative",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe primary purpose of the Recruitment and Admissions Representative is to generate inquiries for Park University and support incoming students in navigating through the entire enrollment process to increase likelihood of attendance. The Recruitment and Admissions Representative works to grow brand awareness and student interest in Park University to yield a desired number of inquiries and applicants annually.  This role will also work to maximize the number of students that start at the University. The Recruitment and Admissions Representative will identify potential students who want to start or further their education at Park University as well as initiate and nurture external and internal relationships that influence potential student decision making and increase the likelihood of student attendance. Position Accountabilities Deliv er enthusiastic Park University   presentations   and   Gilbert Campus   tours .   This position will have goals in relation to the number   of external connections   and   campus   tours   for the recruitment period.    Collect inquiries from all outreach efforts and input on a daily basis.   This position will   work with supervisor to solidify   goals in relation to the number of   appointments,   i nquiries,   admits   and student starts   for   each   recruitment period .        Provide   direction and support necessary to increase   likelihood   of student attendance and   enable students to   prepare for their first semester of class. This includes coordinating with   multiple   office s   effectively   to support the students’ progress, questions, and paperwork.   Build   and implement   a strategy and schedule that will create and foster relationships   to grow brand awareness and generate stude nt interest   in   Park   University.   This   requires   research   and initiative .     Provide on-campus   ( including partner-campus or multi-campus )   communication   with prospective students through phone calls, school visits,   appointments,   emails , text   messages   and other   methods   to   build relationships and   assist   th em with the application and enrollment process   on a daily basis .    There will be specific seasonal commitments for outbound contact work   and events   which   includes   evenings and weekends .     Promotes and   represent s   the university   at   fairs and recruiting   events as approved by the   supervisor.   Responsible for inquiry generation and   expected to provide student   support throughout the enrollment process from inquiry   to day   ten   of   the   student’s start term.   Communication and   student engagement   will be extremely important w hen transitioning students from   non-matriculated to   a   matriculated status .     This includes   attending, hosting, and executing   open house and orientation events,   data entry   using the University CRM   to   assure students are a dmitted and attend   Park.    This position will cross collaborate with athletic coaches   support necessary to increase   likelihood   of student athlete attendance and enable students to prepare for their first semester of class.   Position Requirements: Bachelor’s   d egree   required     The ability to be self-motivated while performing a number of different tasks .      Must be able t o do research and detailed work .   Preference given to candidates with advising, marketing, or sales experience.   Highly flexible, creative, and able to adapt to new project demands.   Strong   problem - solving   skills and strong attention to detail.   Preference given to candidates with working knowledge and experience with a wide range of computer technology such as Microsoft Office (Word, PowerPoint, and Excel), databases,   telephony   and constituent relationship management (CRM) systems.   Must   be a ble to use specialized software ,   such as Sale s f orce.   Strong presentation and public speaking skills .   Strong interpersonal and written communication skills .   Able to work on a non-traditional schedule, specifically evenings and weekends.   Access to reliable transportation and the ability to meet the requirements   to be   an approved Park University vehicle operator.   Reside   in the assigned territory.   Founded in 1875, Park University is a private, liberal arts university. Park’s flagship campus is located in the Kansas City suburb of Parkville, Missouri, on the bluffs overlooking the Missouri River.  We offer an excellent benefits package including health, dental, and life insurance, retirement plan, and tuition-paid undergraduate classes for employees and dependents. Park University is an equal-opportunity employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Qualified applicants must upload a resume and cover letter that includes salary requirements."
    },
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Parkville-MO/Lead-School-Certifying-Official_JR100559": {
      "title": "Lead School Certifying Official",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Lead School Certifying Official (SCO) works with Park University staff, faculty, and students to ensure that Military and Veteran student’s experiences align with the vision, mission, and core values of Park University. The Lead SCO works with the Senior Director of Campus Center Operations and the Warrior Center SCO team to ensure all Veteran Affairs educational certifications and invoices are submitted in a timely and accurate manner. The Lead SCHO assists the military and veteran market by providing expertise in VA Educational benefits, record keeping, analysis, and training of staff. Position Accountabilities Accountabilities 1. Research and Analysis (15%) - Serve as a student information specialist with a primary focus on day-to-day operations at Park Home, Online, and select Campus Centers. Performs regular statistical data research of VA certifications, invoices and overall portfolios for each of these campus centers. Engages with University staff to educate on VA debts and VA regulatory expectations. Perform statistical data compilation on Military and Veteran Educational benefits and develops solutions or alternate methods of proceeding as required. Prepare reports of findings and share data graphically and translating complex findings into written text to educate internal University stakeholders. 2. Processing Records Information (25%)- Manage student records and correspondence with Veteran Affairs in order to maximize efficiency and minimize any errors in accounting, invoicing or documentation. Compile, audit, and verify information within student records for Veteran Affairs Educational Compliance surveys/inspections with no major deficiencies. Ensure a 95% accuracy rate by conducting periodic internal reviews of all military and Veteran student files. Manage department records and data and maintain financial records of Global Warrior Center. 3. Prepare and Monitor Files (25%) - Gather data and prepare reports of findings of student files to include validating degree audits and tuition and fee rates to ensure students are certified correctly for VA Educational benefits. Collect and properly process required Military and Veteran student documentation to ensure student files are updated and correct. Monitor student information system for accurate reporting of student funding, tuition rates, and military status. Assists internal and external auditors and conducts reviews of student accounts. 4. Monitor Market Trends and Changes (15%) -Monitor and communicate changes in policy, trends, and information of Veteran Affairs Educational benefit fiscal policies and procedures. Monitor federal and non-federal funding regulations for changes to policy and regulation. Provide information to the University at large on academic compliance issues and requirements related to these changes. 5. Liaison (15%)- Establish and maintain effective and coordinated working relationships with local, state, and federal agencies and entities that serve Veteran students of Park University. Provide invoicing and accounting information to Vocational Rehabilitation counselors and Park University accounting personnel in a timely manner to ensure prompt payment for tuition, fees and book purchases of students. 6. Training (5%) - Provide training to Park University faculty and staff members on Military VA Educational benefits to include the application process, and the process of certification of all Military and Veteran students. Scope The Lead SCO oversees delivered services and certification of educational benefits of all Military and Veteran students for the Campus Center, Parkville, Gilbert, and Distance populations. The Lead SCO coordinates with the Senior Director of Campus Center Operations and student work studies to ensure all required invoicing, reporting, and daily clerical tasks are completed in a timely manner. Responsible for daily operations and hospitality. Organization The Military and Veteran Funding Analyst reports to the Senior Director of Campus Center Operations. This position may oversee part-time VA student work study students. Challenges and Opportunities Position Requirements: · Bachelor’s degree required. Master’s degree preferred. · Two years of related experience required. · Experience using Tungsten invoicing portal. · Experience using IBM Cognos data analysis software, Microsoft Outlook, Google Drive, Microsoft Excel communication and data management software and Salesforce customer relationship software. · Proficiency in creating reports, sorting and organizing market data sets, and the ability to explain results. · Ability to prepare research outcomes from data reports and manage multiple data sets while maintaining quality assurance. · Capacity to updating and maintaining personnel records while maintaining operational security of student personally identifiable information. · Experience in resolving payment issues between multiple parties. · Ability to effectively organize, plan, and prioritize various tasks. · Ability to pivot between interpersonal communication and problem solving and data entry tasks. · The successful candidate will have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and cultures. · Applicants should have strong interpersonal communication skills, and cross-cultural sensitivity. Physical Requirements · Physical ability and flexible schedule to travel to Park University campus centers located in 21 states. · Physical ability to operate computer, software, and telephone as needed for meetings with distance students, staff, and faculty. · Ability to navigate the Parkville campus (including academic and commercial underground, residential facilities with no elevators, Labor Hall, and other buildings) as needed to meet with faculty, staff, and students. Ability to provide workshops and facilitate meetings – face-to-face and online. Founded in 1875, Park University is a private, liberal arts university. Park’s flagship campus is located in the Kansas City suburb of Parkville, Missouri, on the bluffs overlooking the Missouri River.  We offer an excellent benefits package including health, dental, and life insurance, retirement plan, and tuition-paid undergraduate classes for employees and dependents. Park University is an equal-opportunity employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Qualified applicants must upload a resume and cover letter that includes salary requirements."
    },
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Parkville-MO/Adjunct-Instructor---Nursing-Clinical-Adjunct_JR100018": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor - Nursing Clinical Adjunct",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-01-08\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAppointments are made on a term-by-term basis. Adjunct faculty are required to successfully complete an online Canvas LMS orientation course before being scheduled, as well as other training if required by the department. This is a face to face course. Local applicants only.   Click on Park University Locations for more information on our campus centers. Click on Park University’s Catalog for more information on programs and courses. To ensure timely submission of your credentials, qualified applicants should apply following the specific instructions noted in each job posting. For all positions, a Masters Degree in the relevant field is required, along with related work and/or academic experience. For most postings, a Ph.D. or other terminal degree is preferred. Park University is an Equal Opportunity Employer encouraging applications from women and minorities. The university will recruit and employ qualified personnel and will provide equal opportunities during employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability or status as a qualified protected veteran. Click   here   to view Park University’s EEOC and related policies. Please Note: Park University participates in E-Verify for all positions at all campus center locations nationwide. The Ellen Finley Earhart Department of Nursing at Park University invites applicants to apply for a Clinical Adjunct Faculty position. The clinical adjunct faculty is a valued member of our Nursing Program team. They are responsible for facilitating student learning in a variety of clinical care areas, grading of student learning assessments, collaborating with department faculty, and working with nursing unit staff and patients to assure the safety and quality of our program clinical course work. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s of Science in Nursing (BSN) 3 years of RN experience in the last 5 years Completion of the MHA clinical adjunct academy Unencumbered RN License in Missouri or a multistate license Current American Heart Association BLS certification for the Health Care Provider Positive Employer Evaluations Course Description Our clinical rotations vary depending on clinical placement availability with our clinical partners, as well as the clinical day hours vary by course. Our clinical partners are located throughout the Greater Kansas City area and St. Joseph, MO. North Kansas City Hospital NUR320 Fundamentals Clinicals Saturday Sessions NUR335 Adult Heath I NUR435 Adult Health II (critical care)  St Luke’s East NUR335 Adult Heath I St Luke’s North NUR335 Adult Heath I Signature Psychiatric Hospital at North Kansas City NUR356 Mental Health  ​Signature Psychiatric Hospital at Liberty ​NUR356 Mental Health University of Kansas NUR435 Adult Health II (critical care)"
    },
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Cheyenne-WY/Adjunct-Instructor----Mathematics-MA102--MA120--MA125_JR100003": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor -- Mathematics MA102, MA120, MA125",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-12-18\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAppointments are made on a term-by-term basis. Adjunct faculty are required to successfully complete an online Canvas LMS orientation course before being scheduled, as well as other training if required by the department. This is an on-site blended/hybrid course, students attend class in person 60% of the time and complete the remaining 40% online through Park’s Canvas Learning Management System.   Local applicants only please.   A background check and government security clearance will be required to get on base.   Click on Park University Locations for more information on our campus centers. Click on Park University’s Catalog for more information on programs and courses. To ensure timely submission of your credentials, qualified applicants should apply following the specific instructions noted in each job posting. For all positions, a Masters Degree in the relevant field is required, along with related work and/or academic experience. For most postings, a Ph.D. or other terminal degree is preferred. Park University is an Equal Opportunity Employer encouraging applications from women and minorities. The university will recruit and employ qualified personnel and will provide equal opportunities during employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability or status as a qualified protected veteran. Click   here   to view Park University’s EEOC and related policies. Please Note: Park University participates in E-Verify for all positions at all campus center locations nationwide. Minimum Qualifications MA102 Introductory Algebra Master’s Degree in Mathematics related field. MA120 Basic Concepts of Statistics Masters in Mathematics or a Masters in Applied Mathematics. Candidates with a Masters in Statistics, Actuarial Science, Finance, or Economics will also be considered. MA125 Intermediate Algebra Masters in Mathematics or Applied Mathematics. Candidates with a Master’s degree in Statistics, Physics, Mathematical Education, Operations Research, Civil Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Finance, Actuarial Science or Economics will also be considered. Course Description MA102 Introductory Algebra This developmental course prepares students to complete Parks Liberal Education mathematics requirement. Topics include integer arithmetic, basic algebraic equations, rational numbers, percentages, and basic graphing.  MA120 Basic Concepts of Statistics A development of certain basic concepts in probability and statistics that are pertinent to most disciplines. Topics include: probability models, discrete random variables, normal distributions, confidence intervals, and hypothesis testing. MA125 Intermediate Algebra This course provides a transition into college level Mathematics courses. Topics include the real number system, basic operations of algebra, linear, quadratic and rational equations, inequalities, radicals and exponents, and systems of equations."
    },
