    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ParkUniversityCareers/job/Parkville-MO/Writing-Center-and-English-Language-Learner-Services-Coordinator_JR100567": {
      "title": "Writing Center and English Language Learner Services Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSince its founding in 1875, the diversity of our students has been central to the learning experience at Park University. In addition to serving traditionally aged, adult and military students, the University community includes a significant number of international students and permanent residents for whom English is not a native language. Reporting to the Director of Academic Retention Initiatives, this position coordinates the services Park provides to these English Language Learners. The purpose of this position is to coordinate services for all Park students who need specialized assistance in reading, speaking, and writing English for their Park University classes. These services include one-to-one and group tutoring, course-embedded tutoring, academic mentoring, and consulting with staff and faculty across the University. Position Accountabilities Coordinate Writing and ELL academic support services for undergraduate and graduate students across the Park University network, including training of professional and peer tutors and mentors Plan, develop, and implement a strategic plan that focuses on providing broad support for all Park students in writing and English language learning. Hiring, training, scheduling, and oversight of undergraduate/graduate peer tutoring staff and professional tutors in the Writing Center, for all modalities: Parkville, Gilbert, Campus Centers and Online. Create and present training and support resources to faculty in collaboration with academic program administrators and leaders within student life, student services, international education, writing across the curriculum, and faculty development programs Management of the day-to-day operations of the Writing Center, including overseeing the physical writing center (online writing center, and website; coordinating student orientation sessions and writing workshops; and creating various student and faculty writing resources. Development of innovative programming based on reflective assessment of the Writing Center and its services. Support of undergraduate student research and community engagement aligned with the Writing Center’s strategic plan. Coordination of promotion of services to students and faculty in conjunction with the other services in the Academic and Career Success Center Oversee the development, implementation, and continuous review of policies and practices of the Writing Center, including an assessment plan. Collaboration with academic departments and other units on campus, including the Park Writes, Office of International Programs, First Year Writing Program and Transformational Teaching and Learning Center. Oversee and train Writing and tutors and implement strategic writing and oral communication support for international and non-native English speakers. Beyond academic support, help students understand university policies and how to navigate course expectations. Perform other duties as assigned. Position Requirements: Master’s degree in English/Composition and Rhetoric, or related field with 3-5 years of professional experience working with students in an educational setting. Candidates with less experience may be considered, providing they have an earned specialized training in Writing Tutoring, ELL, English with ELL, ESL, TESOL, or related field Demonstrated understanding of best practices in tutoring writing, based on current writing center pedagogy and Writing Across the Curriculum philosophy. Analytical and organizational skills to understand, assess, and contribute to the development of programs and services Strong communication skills, both oral and written communication, to effectively interact with student, staff, and faculty stakeholders Cross-cultural knowledge, awareness, and empathy to facilitate student, staff, and faculty development Knowledge of higher education norms and expectations for student privacy and non-discrimination Preferred A minimum of two years of relevant Writing Center experience. Experience teaching university-level composition courses. A minor or certification in Teachers of English to Speakers of Other Languages (TESOL) to support diverse, multilingual student population. Scholarship in the field of Composition & Rhetoric, with emphasis in writing center theory and practice. Demonstrated efficacy as a teacher/tutor of undergraduate writers. Founded in 1875, Park University is a private, liberal arts university. Park’s flagship campus is located in the Kansas City suburb of Parkville, Missouri, on the bluffs overlooking the Missouri River.  We offer an excellent benefits package including health, dental, and life insurance, retirement plan, and tuition-paid undergraduate classes for employees and dependents. Park University is an equal-opportunity employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Qualified applicants must upload a resume and cover letter that includes salary requirements."
    },
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ParkUniversityCareers/job/Parkville-MO/Return-of-Title-IV-Specialist_JR100536": {
      "title": "Return of Title IV Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-10\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Return to Title IV Specialist is a role within our Financial Aid division of Student Financial Services. This role is responsible for understanding and maintaining compliance within the function of Return of Title IV. This position is responsible for reviewing and understanding Federal Methodology as it pertains to R2T4, leading the R2T4 team within SFA in the areas of Return of Title IV adjustments, Reaffirmations, lender notifications, and “WF” grade report. Will have full working knowledge of all aspects of the drop and withdraw process; Will have full working knowledge of the complexities of R2T4 decision making in a module-heavy environment; Oversees completion of daily workload and resolves student issues when they require special handling; Manages the Satisfactory Academic Progress Appeal process from start to finish, making professional judgement decisions on these appeals independently; Assists other staff in the absence of the Associate Director, ensures completion of scheduled tasks within assigned deadlines, and assists in achieving departmental and organizational goals. This position is data-heavy with a full working knowledge of excel required. Position Accountabilities Maintaining compliance within the Return of Title IV (R2T4) function in a module based environment Leading the Return of Title IV team to ensure that goals and deadlines are met within the allowed error rate of less than 5% Processing the Return of Title IV calculations and aid adjustments Ensuring the integrity of the add/drop data and integration of that data into PowerFaids Processing of “WF” report at end of each session to process R2T4 on students who fail due to not completing the term Managing the reaffirmation process for students returning to attendance within a semester Ensure adjustments and returns are completed in a timely manner compliant with federal regulations Maintain professional working relationship with Registrar and Student Account departments Manages the Satisfactory Academic Progress Appeal process from start to finish, performing professional judgement decisions independently, working with students, Academic Success Center, and academic advisors to ensure student success following an appeal Assists Student Financial Aid Operations team in the absence of the Associate Director; this requires full knowledge of Title IV regulations and how they impact all functional areas of the financial aid office Other duties as assigned Position Requirements: Bachelor’s Degree required as position is compliance based. Previous experience in Return to Title IV is desired. Ability to work within complex data systems (CX/Jenzabar, PowerFaids). Expected to have a thorough ability to use Excel to manage data (ability to manipulate and interpret data using v-lookup, pivot tables, etc.). Leadership characteristics are required with the ability to hold self and coworkers to high standards in accuracy, deadlines, output, and compliance. Ability to train coworkers in Return to Title IV and other areas of expertise Ability to resolve problems and communicate professionally orally and in writing. Excellent interpersonal skills and ability to maintain good working relationships with outside departments. Ideal candidate would be committed to learning all aspects of the operations of Park Student Financial Aid. Strong orientation toward a high volume and fast-paced environment with demonstrated experience in compliance. Must be able to maintain exceptional level of accuracy while meeting tight deadlines. Previous experience in financial aid or equivalent combination of education and experience is required. Previous experience in Return to Title IV is desired Ability to work independently and make professional judgement decisions on SAP Appeals Ability to multitask, organize and establish priorities are required. Founded in 1875, Park University is a private, liberal arts university. Park’s flagship campus is located in the Kansas City suburb of Parkville, Missouri, on the bluffs overlooking the Missouri River.  We offer an excellent benefits package including health, dental, and life insurance, retirement plan, and tuition-paid undergraduate classes for employees and dependents. Park University is an equal-opportunity employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Qualified applicants must upload a resume and cover letter that includes salary requirements."
    },
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ParkUniversityCareers/job/Gilbert-AZ/Recruitment-and-Admissions-Representative_JR100564": {
      "title": "Recruitment and Admissions Representative",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe primary purpose of the Recruitment and Admissions Representative is to generate inquiries for Park University and support incoming students in navigating through the entire enrollment process to increase likelihood of attendance. The Recruitment and Admissions Representative works to grow brand awareness and student interest in Park University to yield a desired number of inquiries and applicants annually.  This role will also work to maximize the number of students that start at the University. The Recruitment and Admissions Representative will identify potential students who want to start or further their education at Park University as well as initiate and nurture external and internal relationships that influence potential student decision making and increase the likelihood of student attendance. Position Accountabilities Deliv er enthusiastic Park University   presentations   and   Gilbert Campus   tours .   This position will have goals in relation to the number   of external connections   and   campus   tours   for the recruitment period.    Collect inquiries from all outreach efforts and input on a daily basis.   This position will   work with supervisor to solidify   goals in relation to the number of   appointments,   i nquiries,   admits   and student starts   for   each   recruitment period .        Provide   direction and support necessary to increase   likelihood   of student attendance and   enable students to   prepare for their first semester of class. This includes coordinating with   multiple   office s   effectively   to support the students’ progress, questions, and paperwork.   Build   and implement   a strategy and schedule that will create and foster relationships   to grow brand awareness and generate stude nt interest   in   Park   University.   This   requires   research   and initiative .     Provide on-campus   ( including partner-campus or multi-campus )   communication   with prospective students through phone calls, school visits,   appointments,   emails , text   messages   and other   methods   to   build relationships and   assist   th em with the application and enrollment process   on a daily basis .    There will be specific seasonal commitments for outbound contact work   and events   which   includes   evenings and weekends .     Promotes and   represent s   the university   at   fairs and recruiting   events as approved by the   supervisor.   Responsible for inquiry generation and   expected to provide student   support throughout the enrollment process from inquiry   to day   ten   of   the   student’s start term.   Communication and   student engagement   will be extremely important w hen transitioning students from   non-matriculated to   a   matriculated status .     This includes   attending, hosting, and executing   open house and orientation events,   data entry   using the University CRM   to   assure students are a dmitted and attend   Park.    This position will cross collaborate with athletic coaches   support necessary to increase   likelihood   of student athlete attendance and enable students to prepare for their first semester of class.   Position Requirements: Bachelor’s   d egree   required     The ability to be self-motivated while performing a number of different tasks .      Must be able t o do research and detailed work .   Preference given to candidates with advising, marketing, or sales experience.   Highly flexible, creative, and able to adapt to new project demands.   Strong   problem - solving   skills and strong attention to detail.   Preference given to candidates with working knowledge and experience with a wide range of computer technology such as Microsoft Office (Word, PowerPoint, and Excel), databases,   telephony   and constituent relationship management (CRM) systems.   Must   be a ble to use specialized software ,   such as Sale s f orce.   Strong presentation and public speaking skills .   Strong interpersonal and written communication skills .   Able to work on a non-traditional schedule, specifically evenings and weekends.   Access to reliable transportation and the ability to meet the requirements   to be   an approved Park University vehicle operator.   Reside   in the assigned territory.   Founded in 1875, Park University is a private, liberal arts university. Park’s flagship campus is located in the Kansas City suburb of Parkville, Missouri, on the bluffs overlooking the Missouri River.  We offer an excellent benefits package including health, dental, and life insurance, retirement plan, and tuition-paid undergraduate classes for employees and dependents. Park University is an equal-opportunity employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Qualified applicants must upload a resume and cover letter that includes salary requirements."
    },
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ParkUniversityCareers/job/Parkville-MO/Lead-School-Certifying-Official_JR100559": {
      "title": "Lead School Certifying Official",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Lead School Certifying Official (SCO) works with Park University staff, faculty, and students to ensure that Military and Veteran student’s experiences align with the vision, mission, and core values of Park University. The Lead SCO works with the Senior Director of Campus Center Operations and the Warrior Center SCO team to ensure all Veteran Affairs educational certifications and invoices are submitted in a timely and accurate manner. The Lead SCHO assists the military and veteran market by providing expertise in VA Educational benefits, record keeping, analysis, and training of staff. Position Accountabilities Accountabilities 1. Research and Analysis (15%) - Serve as a student information specialist with a primary focus on day-to-day operations at Park Home, Online, and select Campus Centers. Performs regular statistical data research of VA certifications, invoices and overall portfolios for each of these campus centers. Engages with University staff to educate on VA debts and VA regulatory expectations. Perform statistical data compilation on Military and Veteran Educational benefits and develops solutions or alternate methods of proceeding as required. Prepare reports of findings and share data graphically and translating complex findings into written text to educate internal University stakeholders. 2. Processing Records Information (25%)- Manage student records and correspondence with Veteran Affairs in order to maximize efficiency and minimize any errors in accounting, invoicing or documentation. Compile, audit, and verify information within student records for Veteran Affairs Educational Compliance surveys/inspections with no major deficiencies. Ensure a 95% accuracy rate by conducting periodic internal reviews of all military and Veteran student files. Manage department records and data and maintain financial records of Global Warrior Center. 3. Prepare and Monitor Files (25%) - Gather data and prepare reports of findings of student files to include validating degree audits and tuition and fee rates to ensure students are certified correctly for VA Educational benefits. Collect and properly process required Military and Veteran student documentation to ensure student files are updated and correct. Monitor student information system for accurate reporting of student funding, tuition rates, and military status. Assists internal and external auditors and conducts reviews of student accounts. 4. Monitor Market Trends and Changes (15%) -Monitor and communicate changes in policy, trends, and information of Veteran Affairs Educational benefit fiscal policies and procedures. Monitor federal and non-federal funding regulations for changes to policy and regulation. Provide information to the University at large on academic compliance issues and requirements related to these changes. 5. Liaison (15%)- Establish and maintain effective and coordinated working relationships with local, state, and federal agencies and entities that serve Veteran students of Park University. Provide invoicing and accounting information to Vocational Rehabilitation counselors and Park University accounting personnel in a timely manner to ensure prompt payment for tuition, fees and book purchases of students. 6. Training (5%) - Provide training to Park University faculty and staff members on Military VA Educational benefits to include the application process, and the process of certification of all Military and Veteran students. Scope The Lead SCO oversees delivered services and certification of educational benefits of all Military and Veteran students for the Campus Center, Parkville, Gilbert, and Distance populations. The Lead SCO coordinates with the Senior Director of Campus Center Operations and student work studies to ensure all required invoicing, reporting, and daily clerical tasks are completed in a timely manner. Responsible for daily operations and hospitality. Organization The Military and Veteran Funding Analyst reports to the Senior Director of Campus Center Operations. This position may oversee part-time VA student work study students. Challenges and Opportunities Position Requirements: · Bachelor’s degree required. Master’s degree preferred. · Two years of related experience required. · Experience using Tungsten invoicing portal. · Experience using IBM Cognos data analysis software, Microsoft Outlook, Google Drive, Microsoft Excel communication and data management software and Salesforce customer relationship software. · Proficiency in creating reports, sorting and organizing market data sets, and the ability to explain results. · Ability to prepare research outcomes from data reports and manage multiple data sets while maintaining quality assurance. · Capacity to updating and maintaining personnel records while maintaining operational security of student personally identifiable information. · Experience in resolving payment issues between multiple parties. · Ability to effectively organize, plan, and prioritize various tasks. · Ability to pivot between interpersonal communication and problem solving and data entry tasks. · The successful candidate will have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and cultures. · Applicants should have strong interpersonal communication skills, and cross-cultural sensitivity. Physical Requirements · Physical ability and flexible schedule to travel to Park University campus centers located in 21 states. · Physical ability to operate computer, software, and telephone as needed for meetings with distance students, staff, and faculty. · Ability to navigate the Parkville campus (including academic and commercial underground, residential facilities with no elevators, Labor Hall, and other buildings) as needed to meet with faculty, staff, and students. Ability to provide workshops and facilitate meetings – face-to-face and online. Founded in 1875, Park University is a private, liberal arts university. Park’s flagship campus is located in the Kansas City suburb of Parkville, Missouri, on the bluffs overlooking the Missouri River.  We offer an excellent benefits package including health, dental, and life insurance, retirement plan, and tuition-paid undergraduate classes for employees and dependents. Park University is an equal-opportunity employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Qualified applicants must upload a resume and cover letter that includes salary requirements."
    },
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ParkUniversityCareers/job/Parkville-MO/Adjunct-Instructor---Nursing-Clinical-Adjunct_JR100018": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor - Nursing Clinical Adjunct",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-01-08\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAppointments are made on a term-by-term basis. Adjunct faculty are required to successfully complete an online Canvas LMS orientation course before being scheduled, as well as other training if required by the department. This is a face to face course. Local applicants only.   Click on Park University Locations for more information on our campus centers. Click on Park University’s Catalog for more information on programs and courses. To ensure timely submission of your credentials, qualified applicants should apply following the specific instructions noted in each job posting. For all positions, a Masters Degree in the relevant field is required, along with related work and/or academic experience. For most postings, a Ph.D. or other terminal degree is preferred. Park University is an Equal Opportunity Employer encouraging applications from women and minorities. The university will recruit and employ qualified personnel and will provide equal opportunities during employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability or status as a qualified protected veteran. Click   here   to view Park University’s EEOC and related policies. Please Note: Park University participates in E-Verify for all positions at all campus center locations nationwide. The Ellen Finley Earhart Department of Nursing at Park University invites applicants to apply for a Clinical Adjunct Faculty position. The clinical adjunct faculty is a valued member of our Nursing Program team. They are responsible for facilitating student learning in a variety of clinical care areas, grading of student learning assessments, collaborating with department faculty, and working with nursing unit staff and patients to assure the safety and quality of our program clinical course work. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s of Science in Nursing (BSN) 3 years of RN experience in the last 5 years Completion of the MHA clinical adjunct academy Unencumbered RN License in Missouri or a multistate license Current American Heart Association BLS certification for the Health Care Provider Positive Employer Evaluations Course Description Our clinical rotations vary depending on clinical placement availability with our clinical partners, as well as the clinical day hours vary by course. Our clinical partners are located throughout the Greater Kansas City area and St. Joseph, MO. North Kansas City Hospital NUR320 Fundamentals Clinicals Saturday Sessions NUR335 Adult Heath I NUR435 Adult Health II (critical care)  St Luke’s East NUR335 Adult Heath I St Luke’s North NUR335 Adult Heath I Signature Psychiatric Hospital at North Kansas City NUR356 Mental Health  ​Signature Psychiatric Hospital at Liberty ​NUR356 Mental Health University of Kansas NUR435 Adult Health II (critical care)"
    },
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ParkUniversityCareers/job/Cheyenne-WY/Adjunct-Instructor----Mathematics-MA102--MA120--MA125_JR100003": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor -- Mathematics MA102, MA120, MA125",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-12-18\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAppointments are made on a term-by-term basis. Adjunct faculty are required to successfully complete an online Canvas LMS orientation course before being scheduled, as well as other training if required by the department. This is an on-site blended/hybrid course, students attend class in person 60% of the time and complete the remaining 40% online through Park’s Canvas Learning Management System.   Local applicants only please.   A background check and government security clearance will be required to get on base.   Click on Park University Locations for more information on our campus centers. Click on Park University’s Catalog for more information on programs and courses. To ensure timely submission of your credentials, qualified applicants should apply following the specific instructions noted in each job posting. For all positions, a Masters Degree in the relevant field is required, along with related work and/or academic experience. For most postings, a Ph.D. or other terminal degree is preferred. Park University is an Equal Opportunity Employer encouraging applications from women and minorities. The university will recruit and employ qualified personnel and will provide equal opportunities during employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability or status as a qualified protected veteran. Click   here   to view Park University’s EEOC and related policies. Please Note: Park University participates in E-Verify for all positions at all campus center locations nationwide. Minimum Qualifications MA102 Introductory Algebra Master’s Degree in Mathematics related field. MA120 Basic Concepts of Statistics Masters in Mathematics or a Masters in Applied Mathematics. Candidates with a Masters in Statistics, Actuarial Science, Finance, or Economics will also be considered. MA125 Intermediate Algebra Masters in Mathematics or Applied Mathematics. Candidates with a Master’s degree in Statistics, Physics, Mathematical Education, Operations Research, Civil Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Finance, Actuarial Science or Economics will also be considered. Course Description MA102 Introductory Algebra This developmental course prepares students to complete Parks Liberal Education mathematics requirement. Topics include integer arithmetic, basic algebraic equations, rational numbers, percentages, and basic graphing.  MA120 Basic Concepts of Statistics A development of certain basic concepts in probability and statistics that are pertinent to most disciplines. Topics include: probability models, discrete random variables, normal distributions, confidence intervals, and hypothesis testing. MA125 Intermediate Algebra This course provides a transition into college level Mathematics courses. Topics include the real number system, basic operations of algebra, linear, quadratic and rational equations, inequalities, radicals and exponents, and systems of equations."
    },
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ParkUniversityCareers/job/Parkville-Campus/Scholarship-Coordinator_JR100584": {
      "title": "Scholarship Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe purpose of this position is to ensure the effective, accurate, and student-centered administration of the University's scholarship programs while providing exceptional service to students and campus stakeholders. The Scholarship Coordinator works collaboratively with university departments to promote consistent scholarship processes, maintain the integrity of scholarship programs, and support institutional efforts to enhance student access, affordability, and success. Position Accountabilities •    Coordinate the day-to-day administration of institutional scholarship programs. •    Assist with the scholarship application, review, awarding, renewal, and disbursement processes. •    Ensure scholarship awards are processed accurately, timely, and in accordance with University policies and established procedures. •    Maintain accurate scholarship records within the student information system and other applicable software. •    Review scholarship applications and verify eligibility based on established criteria. •    Prepare scholarship materials and provide administrative support for scholarship committees. •    Review scholarship renewal eligibility, including GPA, enrollment status, and other established requirements. •    Process scholarship revisions resulting from enrollment changes or other eligibility updates. •    Assist the Advancement Office with the administration of privately funded scholarship programs. •    Help ensure donor restrictions and scholarship criteria are accurately applied. •    Collect and maintain scholarship recipient information to support donor stewardship activities. •    Provide administrative support for the athletic scholarship awarding process in collaboration with Athletics and Financial Aid. •    Compile routine reports related to scholarship awards, utilization, and recipient data. •    Maintain accurate records to support reporting, audits, and compliance requirements. •    Assist in documenting and maintaining scholarship policies, procedures, and operational guidelines. •    Provide scholarship information and customer service to prospective and current students, families, faculty, and staff. •    Develop and maintain effective working relationships with Admissions, Advancement, Academic Affairs, Athletics, Financial Aid, and other campus partners. •    Coordinate with academic departments regarding department-specific scholarship processes. •    Participate on scholarship committees and other meetings as assigned.   Position Requirements: • Bachelor’s Degree required. •    Preference given to candidates with experience in financial aid, scholarships, admissions, or enrollment management. •    Experience working with student information systems, scholarship management software, or relational databases preferred.   •    Demonstrated commitment to providing exceptional customer service and fostering positive relationships with students, families, faculty, and staff. •    Excellent organizational and time management skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment. •    Strong attention to detail and a high level of accuracy in processing records and maintaining confidential information. •    Ability to analyze information, solve problems, and exercise sound judgment in interpreting policies and procedures. •    Ability to work both independently and collaboratively as part of a team. •    Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to interact effectively with individuals from diverse backgrounds. •    Demonstrated ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive information with professionalism and discretion. •    Ability to learn new technologies and adapt to changing processes and priorities. •    Commitment to providing equitable, student-centered service while supporting the University's mission and values. Founded in 1875, Park University is a private, liberal arts university. Park’s flagship campus is located in the Kansas City suburb of Parkville, Missouri, on the bluffs overlooking the Missouri River.  We offer an excellent benefits package including health, dental, and life insurance, retirement plan, and tuition-paid undergraduate classes for employees and dependents. Park University is an equal-opportunity employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Qualified applicants must upload a resume and cover letter that includes salary requirements."
    },
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ParkUniversityCareers/job/Parkville-MO/Executive-Administrative-Assistant-to-Dean-of-Faculty_JR100579": {
      "title": "Executive Administrative Assistant to Dean of Faculty",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Executive Assistant represents the first line of academic and professional excellence for the Dean’s Office. The position serves as a primary point of contact for inquiries and issues that span the five academic divisions at Park. The position provides high-level administrative, operational, and project support to the Dean of Faculty, coordinating complex calendars and meetings, including those with external stakeholders; managing confidential communications and records related to employment; supporting faculty-facing processes; and facilitating cross-divisional collaboration to advance academic priorities and faculty success. Additionally, the position serves to track budget and programmatic data across the five divisions. In addition to serving as the primary administrative liaison between the divisions and Academic Affairs, the position collaborates closely with the Divisional Administrative Services Coordinator to ensure consistency, effectiveness, and effective flow of communication across Academic Affairs, the Dean’s Office, and the Divisions. The Dean’s Executive Administrative Assistant demonstrates professionalism, exercises appropriate judgment and discretion in behavior in all aspects of the work environment, and embraces and exhibits the core values of the University. As the position is involved in personnel matters such as faculty contracts and workloads, maintains strict confidentiality. Position Accountabilities 1. Executive Support, Budget and Operations Management Manage the Dean’s calendar, schedule and coordinate internal and external meetings, and prioritize appointments. Prepare agendas, briefing materials, presentations, and meeting minutes, and track follow-up items for Divisional Associate Deans Council meetings. Screen and triage calls, email, and requests; draft and manage professional correspondence on behalf of the Dean. Maintain files and records (faculty contracts, committee reports, personnel actions) with strict attention to confidentiality and compliance. Help track program accreditation activities across the Divisions to ensure compliance at the University-level in terms of program accreditation actions and statuses. Maintain master calendar of key faculty and student events to facilitate engagement by University leadership. Coordinate travel arrangements, reimbursements, and expense reporting for the Dean and visiting faculty/guests. Serve as budget manager at the Dean level, which includes all budgets supporting cross-divisional functions, such as tracking/reconciling CBA budgeted professional development funds and endowed funds that cross academic divisions. Collect budget requests from the Divisions as part of annual budget preparation, documenting rationales and noting budget items that connect to assessment outcomes. 2. Faculty and Governance Support Assist with full-time faculty recruitment logistics, search committee scheduling, interview coordination, and candidate communications across the Divisions to ensure consistency and timeliness. Support faculty appointment and contract processes by collecting and routing documentation, tracking deadlines, and liaising with HR and Academic Affairs in the preparation of initial contracts and renewals. Coordinate activities related to Dean involvement in faculty evaluations, pre-tenure, tenure and promotion (scheduling, document collection, and recordkeeping). Collect faculty workload data from Divisions, including data related to teaching, advising, and service loads; perform analysis; and flag issues requiring resolution by the Dean and Faculty. Track all Collective Bargaining Agreement related deadlines and actions required of the Dean of Faculty. Maintain repository of Division meting minutes and Associate Dean minutes. Provide administrative support to the University Assessment Committee and other Senate and/or University-level committees, task forces, or working groups as assigned. 3. Projects, Events, and Communication Help plan and execute faculty-focused events, training workshops, and leadership meetings, including room/virtual logistics, materials, etc. Support all data collection, annual assessment, and program review activities involving the Dean of Faculty. Track action items from meetings, follow up with stakeholders, and maintain project timelines. Serve as a professional and responsive liaison between the Dean’s Office and Associate Deans, Program Directors, faculty, staff, students, and external partners. Draft and distribute internal communications, calendar invites, and updates related to cross-divisional initiatives and deadlines. Support strategic initiatives of the Dean (e.g., faculty development programs, cross-divisional initiatives, advancement outreach) and perform research, compilation of materials, and basic analysis as needed. Collate and monitor division strategic initiative plans, produce period reports to track progress and alignment to University goals. 4. External Relations, Partnerships, and Advancement Support Act as the primary administrative contact for the Dean’s external relations activities, including scheduling and coordinating meetings with donors, alumni, industry partners, and community stakeholders. Organize and support advisory group meetings: schedule meetings, prepare agendas and materials, record minutes, track action items, and maintain advisory group records. Arrange and manage Dean’s participation in community, industry, and professional events (registrations, travel, materials, booth or presentation logistics) and prepare post-event summaries and contact follow-ups. Assist in preparing proposals, briefing memos, and outreach materials needed for Advancement to provide to prospective partners and program-level alumni engagement campaigns. Confidential Data Stewardship Handle, store, transmit, and archive confidential student, faculty, and institutional data in compliance with FERPA, data privacy standards, collective bargaining agreements, and University policies. Exercise discretion and sound judgment in managing sensitive personnel, student conduct, academic, financial, and accreditation-related information. Maintain secure electronic and physical filing systems and ensure appropriate access controls and records retention practices. Position Requirements: Associate’s degree required; bachelor’s degree preferred. Minimum of five years of progressively responsible administrative experience, preferably in higher education or a complex organizational environment; experience serving senior academic leaders strongly preferred. Exceptional organizational skills, attention to detail, and ability to manage competing priorities and confidential information. Strong written and oral communication skills; professional interpersonal presence. Proficiency with Microsoft 365 suite, calendar systems, and virtual meeting platforms (Zoom or equivalent). Proficient with platforms such as Teams; familiarity with enterprise LMS (e.g., Canvas) preferred. Familiarity with Student Information Systems and basic data/reporting tools; willingness to learn new data systems and processes. Demonstrated ability to coordinate complex schedules, plan internal and external events, and produce high-quality documents and presentations. Strong problem-solving skills, discretion, and the ability to work independently and as part of cross-functional teams. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of academic governance processes, faculty appointment/evaluation workflows, and accreditation-related processes is highly desirable Founded in 1875, Park University is a private, liberal arts university. Park’s flagship campus is located in the Kansas City suburb of Parkville, Missouri, on the bluffs overlooking the Missouri River.  We offer an excellent benefits package including health, dental, and life insurance, retirement plan, and tuition-paid undergraduate classes for employees and dependents. Park University is an equal-opportunity employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Qualified applicants must upload a resume and cover letter that includes salary requirements."
    },
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ParkUniversityCareers/job/Parkville-Campus/Adjunct-Instructor---CIS622-Data-Architecture-for-Business-Analytics_JR100585": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor - CIS622 Data Architecture for Business Analytics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-15\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nAppointments are made on a term-by-term basis. Adjunct faculty are required to successfully complete an online Canvas LMS orientation course before being scheduled, as well as other training if required by the department. This is a face to face course. Local applicants only.   Click on Park University Locations for more information on our campus centers. Click on Park University’s Catalog for more information on programs and courses. To ensure timely submission of your credentials, qualified applicants should apply following the specific instructions noted in each job posting. For all positions, a Masters Degree in the relevant field is required, along with related work and/or academic experience. For most postings, a Ph.D. or other terminal degree is preferred. Park University is an Equal Opportunity Employer encouraging applications from women and minorities. The university will recruit and employ qualified personnel and will provide equal opportunities during employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability or status as a qualified protected veteran. Click   here   to view Park University’s EEOC and related policies. Please Note: Park University participates in E-Verify for all positions at all campus center locations nationwide. Minimum Qualifications Master’s Degree in Business Analytics, Data Science, Statistics, Operations Management, Computer Science, or related fields with 18 credits in quantitative or classes in Analytics. Proficiency in the following areas of Business Analytics, Data Analytics, Predictive Analytics, and related fields. Knowledge of Python or R, and Tableau, and statistical software preferred.  Ph.D. and a minimal of 5 years teaching experience or post-secondary teaching experience is preferred. Resume must be submitted in ACBSP format.  Course Description This course will teach students to identify data sources and datasets relevant to business problems, gather, and manipulate data. Students will learn how to build and use relational, and non-relational databases as well as how to work with standalone datasets, APIs and other formats of data. This course will also focus on the main data manipulation methods such as querying, merging, filtering, and aggregation using various tools and their relation to the analytical solutions to business problems."
    },
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ParkUniversityCareers/job/Parkville-MO/Student-Account-Representative---University-Cashier_JR100588": {
      "title": "Student Account Representative & University Cashier",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nStudent Accounts Representatives make sure the University bills and collects the revenue for tuition and fees charged to students.  The billing portion they may do themselves or approve the work of others.  The University Cashier accepts cash, check and credit or debit card payments for tuition and fees from students via phone calls or in person.  This position is involved in handling cash. Position Accountabilities Position Description – FY 2025-2026 Job Title Student Account Representative & University Cashier Date July 1, 2025 Department Finance & Administration FLSA Non-Exempt Supervisor Director of Student Accounts Employment Status Full Time   Purpose:       Student Accounts Representatives make sure the University bills and collects the revenue for tuition and fees charged to students.  The billing portion they may do themselves or approve the work of others.  The University Cashier accepts cash, check and credit or debit card payments for tuition and fees from students via phone calls or in person.  This position is involved in handling cash.   Accountabilities: Monitor and respond timely and accurately to student and staff calls and emails Cashier window coverage / Accepting student payments Review and approve student refunds Audit and enter third party invoices for the Campus Centers Review tuition adjustments for accuracy following enrollment adjustments Prepare / Send student balance letters Prepare and execute journal entries as needed for student fees, etc. Audit receivables and follow-up as appropriate Meet weekly deadlines Additional duties as assigned   Scope:       Student Accounts Representatives serve all students.  In addition to the largest campus in Parkville, MO, there are approximately 8 other Campus Centers throughout the US and online, with a population totaling nearly 6,000 total students.    Organization:       This position reports to the Director of Student Accounts.   Challenges and Opportunities:       This position is in a fast-paced environment and requires high accuracy as well as a great deal of multitasking.  Exceptional communication skills and excellent customer service skills are necessary to provide the level of student service that is required.  Compliance with privacy laws is required.  The workload cycles with the progression of each term, and there are predictable peaks in work levels.   Position Requirements: Education High school degree or GED is required. A bachelor’s degree in a business-related field is preferred and may be accepted in lieu of direct work experience. Experience 1-3 years of experience in cash handling, customer service, and accounting experience is required. Skills: Strong team-building skills, ability to work well with a wide variety of colleagues and diverse groups.  Ability to maintain professionalism and positive demeanor under pressure. Must be willing to work in a highly structured environment.Most have strong problem-solving abilities, high accuracy and exceptional attention to detail. Solid working knowledge and experience with a wide range of computer technologies such as Microsoft Office® (Word, Excel, Outlook), databases, telephone and digital telecommunication, CRM and online technologies. Ability to work in a virtual environment.Willingness to work flexible and extended hours when needed. Physical Requirements: Individuals should be able to sit for long periods of time at a computer.   Position Requirements: Founded in 1875, Park University is a private, liberal arts university. Park’s flagship campus is located in the Kansas City suburb of Parkville, Missouri, on the bluffs overlooking the Missouri River.  We offer an excellent benefits package including health, dental, and life insurance, retirement plan, and tuition-paid undergraduate classes for employees and dependents. Park University is an equal-opportunity employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Qualified applicants must upload a resume and cover letter that includes salary requirements."
    },
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ParkUniversityCareers/job/Parkville-MO/Adjunct-Faculty---Interior-Design_JR100592": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Interior Design",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAppointments are made on a term-by-term basis. Adjunct faculty are required to successfully complete an online Canvas LMS orientation course before being scheduled, as well as other training if required by the department. This is a face to face course. Local applicants only.   Click on Park University Locations for more information on our campus centers. Click on Park University’s Catalog for more information on programs and courses. To ensure timely submission of your credentials, qualified applicants should apply following the specific instructions noted in each job posting. For all positions, a Masters Degree in the relevant field is required, along with related work and/or academic experience. For most postings, a Ph.D. or other terminal degree is preferred. Park University is an Equal Opportunity Employer encouraging applications from women and minorities. The university will recruit and employ qualified personnel and will provide equal opportunities during employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability or status as a qualified protected veteran. Click   here   to view Park University’s EEOC and related policies. Please Note: Park University participates in E-Verify for all positions at all campus center locations nationwide. Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree or higher in Interior Design or a closely related design field, or a minimum of 18 graduate credit hours in the discipline or subfield relevant to the courses being taught. Candidates should also have a minimum of five years of professional experience in interior design or a closely related field, with demonstrated expertise relevant to the course(s) they will teach. Professional experience should be documented through a résumé and, when appropriate, a professional portfolio. Course Description AR282 Visual Communications I An introduction to basic drafting techniques, terminology, and symbols used in architectural drawings, using drafting equipment, lettering, plan and elevation construction with emphasis on proper line weight, quality, and scale; additionally study materials and fabrication techniques involved in the design and construction of interior details. AR296 Textiles for Interior Design This course explores the nature of man-made and natural materials used to produce textiles for use within the interior design industry. Content includes discussion of fibers, yarns, fabrics, finishes, design methods, construction, and proper application of these materials from technical, environmental and aesthetic approaches. AR289 Fundamentals of Interior Design An exploration of residential space planning problems applying the design process and space planning techniques to projects that emphasizes research and application of global design and the study of different cultures. Includes an intermediate review of life safety codes and accessibility guidelines. AR290 Interior Design Materials and Resources A survey of the materials and finishes utilized in interior applications through lecture, demonstrations, and/or field trips. Various methods of specification and estimation are reviewed, with students researching and assessing performance criteria including environmental ethics and social responsibility. AR382 Drawing Systems I An introduction to the principles and operations of computer generated drawing with an emphasis on producing both 2D (floor plans, elevations, etc.) and 3D (orthographic) drawings using AutoCAD."
    },
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ParkUniversityCareers/job/Parkville-Campus/Assistant-Professor-Business-Analytics_JR100591": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Business Analytics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPark University invites applications for a Full-Time tenure track Assistant Professor position starting in August 1, 2027 The successful candidate will primarily teach in-person, on-campus courses within Park University's Information Systems and Business Analytics programs. Our dynamic business analytics curriculum includes coursework in information systems, data mining, data visualization, predictive analytics, and digital marketing analytics. Students engage in hands-on, applied learning experiences that incorporate statistical analysis, programming, and data visualization tools to solve real-world business challenges. Position Accountabilities Teaching responsibilities will be aligned with the candidate’s academic background and professional expertise. In addition to face-to-face instruction, the teaching load may include online courses. Opportunities to develop and enhance online course offerings may also be available. The standard teaching assignment is four courses per semester. Position Requirements: Qualifications: Ph.D. or D.B.A (ABD or master’s degree considered) in business with a focus on Business Analytics including Information Systems, Data Analytics, or Data Science or a closely related field from a regionally accredited university.  Master’s degree with industry experience may be considered Proficiency in Python, R, SQL, and statistical software. Demonstrated teaching experience at the undergraduate or graduate level. Preferred Qualifications: Academic and/ or industry experience in: database systems data collection from multiple sources, including APIs. Business Analytics Experience teaching online courses Expertise in DevOps, data pipeline design, and cloud computing platforms, such as AWS. Qualified applicants must upload their curriculum vitae, cover letter, teaching philosophy, and professional references.  The cover letter must identify the candidate’s salary expectations. Review of applications begins October 19. Founded in 1875, Park University is a private, liberal arts university. Park’s flagship campus is located in the Kansas City suburb of Parkville, Missouri, on the bluffs overlooking the Missouri River.  We offer an excellent benefits package including health, dental, and life insurance, retirement plan, and tuition-paid undergraduate classes for employees and dependents. Park University is an equal-opportunity employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Qualified applicants must upload a resume and cover letter that includes salary requirements."
    },
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ParkUniversityCareers/job/Parkville-Campus/Academic-and-Athletic-Compliance-Coordinator_JR100587": {
      "title": "Academic and Athletic Compliance Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-17\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThis position carries out compliance functions to ensure compliance with federal, state, and other regulations and to mitigate institutional risk. Under the direction of the Registrar, this position carries out compliance functions, with particular emphasis on enrollment reporting and athletic eligibility. Position Accountabilities Work closely with Registrar to compile, review, analyze, and update student enrollment data to ensure data integrity; submit enrollment reports including enrollment statuses and effective dates, program data, and student demographic information, to National Student Clearinghouse per Department of Education guidelines. Investigate and resolve anomalies and make corrections to report and source data, when applicable. Test any report/data updates for accuracy as federal requirements change. Respond to National Student Loan Database System SSCR reports/data requests. Review all flagged records, research issues, and update records or follow up with students, as needed. Monitor, update, and disseminate data on effective dates for course and session drops/withdrawals based on evidence including academic activity, data logs, and related documentation. Disseminate reports to stakeholders, particularly Financial Aid and VA School Certifying Officials, to ensure consistency across departments and to lay firm foundation for relevant aspects of VA and Title IV compliance audits. Assess athletic eligibility for student athletes in accordance with rules and regulations of the National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics (NAIA) and Park University. In collaboration with the Athletic Director, Faculty Athletic Representative, and Coaches, ensure that athletes meet eligibility requirements for initial and continuing participation each semester. Review high school and college transcripts, NAIA records, and test scores or other documents, to determine eligibility. Alert coaches and athletic staff of eligibility-related issues that may delay or prevent athletic certification. Record, collect, and submit eligibility rosters to NAIA. Assist coaches, athletics staff, and students regarding eligibility. Submit transcripts of current Park students to NAIA Eligibility Center. Collaborate with OIRA and athletic departments to compile and disseminate individual and team athletic data to stakeholders for purposes such as NAIA scholar athlete and scholar team awards.  Collaborate with Enrollment Services, Financial Aid, Accounting, and Warrior Center to evaluate requests for retroactive withdrawals and determine effective dates based on medical, deployment, or other documentation, in accordance with the federal regulations and university policy. Execute administrative withdrawal process, including sending of communication and reports to stakeholders, assessing enrollment and participation records, and processing batch/individual withdrawals. Provide customer service to students and faculty/staff, including responding to phone calls and email inquiries. Assist with office priorities, including transcripts fulfillment, enrollment/degree verification, grading, graduation and degree checks, and course scheduling. Maintain accurate records of programs offered at all campus centers and locations to assist with state reporting. Assist with office projects. Position Requirements: Bachelor’s degree required. Previous higher education experience required. 2 years related experience. Strong proficiency in computer applications, including Microsoft Excel to analyze large data sets. Experience with Jenzabar or an SIS preferred. Detail oriented. Strong analytical skills. Ability to interpret and apply complex rules and regulations. Effective communication skills. Solid judgment, particularly with regard to enforcement of policy and regulations. Knowledge of Family Educational & Rights & Privacy Act regulations. Founded in 1875, Park University is a private, liberal arts university. Park’s flagship campus is located in the Kansas City suburb of Parkville, Missouri, on the bluffs overlooking the Missouri River.  We offer an excellent benefits package including health, dental, and life insurance, retirement plan, and tuition-paid undergraduate classes for employees and dependents. Park University is an equal-opportunity employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Qualified applicants must upload a resume and cover letter that includes salary requirements."
    },
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ParkUniversityCareers/job/Parkville-Campus/Director-Library-Services_JR100581-1": {
      "title": "Director Library Services",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-17\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Director of Library Services provides strategic leadership for all functions of the library, collaborating with faculty and staff across the University to support Park’s mission and student learning outcomes. The Director is responsible for oversight of the Norrington Center, the physical location of the Library on the Parkville flagship campus, as well as the digital resources that serve Park students studying on campuses in six states and online. Position Accountabilities Responsible for defining and articulating the vision, strategic directions, and priorities for the future of the Library and for developing a dynamic environment that values creativity, teamwork, and innovation Oversees the development, delivery, and assessment of library services, resources, and programming in support of student learning. The position requires a commitment to student success and to the provision of excellent service, as well as strengths in outreach, collaboration, supervision, and assessment. Embraces emerging technologies; provides a combination of vision and practical management in response to the emergence of face-to-face, online, and hybrid educational experiences. Advocates on behalf of the Library both inside and outside the university and represents the library at local, state, regional, and national consortia and associations Works closely with administration and faculty to ensure that library resources, services, and programming meet the needs of the entire university community; measures service quality and makes improvements as needed. Serves as the facility supervisor for the Norrington Center, Campanella Gallery manager, and other campus units to ensure a safe and supportive learning environment for students Oversees the Fishburn Archives and processes for records retention and collections management, in collaboration with appropriate administrative offices Serves as project manager for library technology projects, and serves as the main point of contact with vendors Position Requirements: Master’s Degree in Library Science from an ALA-accredited institution. Education or experience in archives management and/or a second master’s or a doctoral degree is preferred but not required. Familiarity with trends and best practices in higher education and academic libraries A track record of progressively more responsible administrative, management, or leadership experience, preferably in an academic library with an emphasis on strategic planning, budget management, staff development, and emerging technologies Demonstrated understanding of and commitment to the core tenets of academic librarianship as articulated by the American Library Association’s Bill of Rights, Intellectual Freedom Principles for Academic Librarians, and Code of Ethics, as well as the Association of College and Research Libraries’ Framework for Information Literacy Strong interpersonal, communication, leadership, and collaboration skills, especially as they apply to the work of building and maintaining a respectful, collegial, and inclusive work environment Proven track record of successfully working with faculty, other department heads, and administrators to develop and deliver services that support teaching, learning, and scholarship Demonstrated leadership and communication techniques that exemplify transparency and accountability, that build trust between and among individuals and groups, and that elicit creativity, commitment, and high performance from employees Proven successes in the development, delivery, and assessment of library collections and services Preferred Qualifications: Experience with program evaluation, assessment, and accreditation practices Demonstrated knowledge of information technology as it relates to libraries, and the ability to effectively communicate with technologists, administration, and library personnel about technology Experience with the development and delivery of library services to distance and online students Ability to perform administrative functions for a range of online information tools and databases Experience developing and implementing user-centered digital projects Founded in 1875, Park University is a private, liberal arts university. Park’s flagship campus is located in the Kansas City suburb of Parkville, Missouri, on the bluffs overlooking the Missouri River.  We offer an excellent benefits package including health, dental, and life insurance, retirement plan, and tuition-paid undergraduate classes for employees and dependents. Park University is an equal-opportunity employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Qualified applicants must upload a resume and cover letter that includes salary requirements."
    },
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ParkUniversityCareers/job/Parkville-Campus/Associate--Director-Student-Financial-Services_JR100593": {
      "title": "Associate  Director Student Financial Services",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-25\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe Associate Director of Financial Aid provides operational leadership for the University’s financial aid and scholarship functions, overseeing day-to-day student service operations, scholarship awarding, workflow management, and an assigned team within Financial Aid. The position ensures financial aid processes are completed accurately, efficiently, and in full compliance with federal, state, institutional, and regulatory requirements while monitoring workloads, delegating responsibilities, supporting budget management, and maintaining effective communication with internal and external constituents. The Assistant/Associate Director also leads the development, implementation, assessment, and continuous improvement of departmental processes and initiatives; supports special projects and staff training; and fosters a collaborative, accountable, and service-oriented team environment. Through strong leadership and sound financial aid administration, the position advances student success, supports University enrollment and organizational goals, and safeguards the integrity and effectiveness of financial aid operations. Position Accountabilities Supervise, develop, and provide ongoing training to assigned Financial Aid team members, establishing expectations for performance, professionalism, accountability, and student service consistent with standards established by the Director of Student Financial Aid. Maintain comprehensive knowledge of federal, state, and institutional financial aid regulations, policies, and best practices to ensure compliance and support the department’s ability to respond effectively to regulatory and operational changes. Monitor financial aid processing workflows and student records using PowerFAIDS, Workday, and other systems to identify incomplete files, processing delays, and service needs; develop and coordinate targeted outreach and resolution strategies. Serve as an escalation point for complex student and family financial aid concerns, resolving issues within established authority and referring appropriate matters to the Director of Student Financial Aid. Manage and monitor the Student Employment budget for Federal Work-Study and institutional student employment programs, including monthly reconciliation and reporting to the Director of Student Financial Aid. Serve as backup to the Student Employment Administrator, supporting the timely and accurate processing, onboarding, and administration of student employees. Assist with the annual development, review, and maintenance of financial aid policies and procedures, ensuring departmental documentation reflects current regulations, institutional policies, and operational practices. Assist with the reconciliation and oversight of federal, state, institutional, and scholarship funds, ensuring awards are accurate, appropriately documented, and administered in accordance with applicable requirements. Provide operational oversight of institutional scholarship programs, including awarding, eligibility review, renewal, reconciliation, and coordination with Admissions, Athletics, Academic Affairs, and other University partners to ensure scholarships are administered consistently and strategically. Coordinate with University Advancement and the Park University Foundation on donor-funded and Foundation scholarships, supporting eligibility review, awarding, reconciliation, stewardship requirements, and effective utilization of available scholarship funds. Partner with Admissions and other University departments to support recruitment, orientation, and enrollment events and provide timely financial aid and scholarship guidance that enhances the prospective and current student experience. Exercise independent judgment and discretion in handling confidential information, analyzing complex situations, resolving operational issues, and making decisions appropriate to the responsibilities and authority of the position. Scope As part of daily operations, the Associate Director will oversee 3-4 staff members who all play a vital part in the loan and scholarship awarding process.  Organization This position will report to the Director of Student Financial Aid.  Positions that report to the Associate Director are Financial Aid Counselors, the Student Employment Administrator and the Scholarship Coordinator. Challenges and Opportunities Must have exceptionally strong communication skills and able to interact effectively with students, administrators, faculty and staff.  Expected to manage multiple projects under time constraints, use critical thinking, work under pressure, and oversee work of others. Position Requirements: ·         Bachelor’s degree required, Master’s Preferred ·         Experience with COD and NSLDS ·         Knowledge of federal financial aid regulations required ·         Knowledge of federal and state financial aid programs and guidelines. ·         Knowledge of department and university policies, procedures, and practices with the ability to answer work related questions. ·         Effective organizational and management skills. ·         Ability to adapt quickly to changes in rules and regulations. ·         Ability to develop and interpret financial data/plans and manage resources. ·         Ability to establish and maintain positive working relationships with other staff at all levels and with diverse student populations. ·         Ability to operate financial aid software programs and external systems and web page content management systems.  ·         Perform assigned responsibilities, duties, and tasks according to established practices and procedures with minimal supervision. ·         Ability to manage interpersonal conflict situations requiring tact, diplomacy and discretion. ·         Other duties as assigned.   Physical Requirements ·         While performing the duties of this job, the employee may sit for long periods of time, occasionally walk and stand; hand dexterity to operate computer; hearing and eyesight for counseling, phone and computer work. Founded in 1875, Park University is a private, liberal arts university. Park’s flagship campus is located in the Kansas City suburb of Parkville, Missouri, on the bluffs overlooking the Missouri River.  We offer an excellent benefits package including health, dental, and life insurance, retirement plan, and tuition-paid undergraduate classes for employees and dependents. Park University is an equal-opportunity employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Qualified applicants must upload a resume and cover letter that includes salary requirements."
    }
  },
